# A push onto a list made in the function is written out: the length is compared with the capacity, the element is stored and the length grows by one.
# LOOP-LABEL: loop #
# LOOP: Int32 b@[[fits]] = Below(b@[[length]], b@{{*}}, {{*}}:HasSpareArrayCapacity)
# LOOP-NEXT: Branch(b@[[fits]], Terminal, {{*}}:HasSpareArrayCapacity)
# LOOP-NEXT: Successors: Then:#{{*}}, Else:Rare:#
# LOOP: Store(b@{{*}}, b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Writes:indexedDoubleProperties, {{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP: Int32 b@[[longer]] = Add(b@[[length]], $1(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP-LABEL: end of loop
# The storage, its capacity and the length stay in registers: only the path that grows the list, which leaves the loop, changes them. The kind of storage is not tested. Nothing is called; the one patchpoint is the poll.
# NONE-LABEL: loop #
# NONE-NOT: Reads:JSObject_butterfly
# NONE-NOT: Reads:Butterfly_vectorLength
# NONE-NOT: Butterfly_publicLength
# NONE-NOT: Reads:JSCell_indexingTypeAndMisc
# NONE-NOT: :CallBuiltin
# NONE-NOT: Register(
# NONE-LABEL: end of loop
